,title,link,text,language,family
0,Stieng language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stieng_language,"January 8, 2026 - In the Austroasiatic scheme, the Bahnaric languages are often cited as being most closely related to the Khmer language. There are noted dialects of Stieng, some of which may not be mutually intelligible. However, due to the lack of widely available research, this article will primarily describe the dialect known as Bulo ...","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
1,"Stieng, Bulo Language (STI) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/sti/,"Bulo Stieng is a stable indigenous language of Vietnam and Cambodia. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
2,Austro-Asiatic | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/231/,"Stieng, Bulo sti, a language of Viet Nam · West Bahnaric 9 · Lavi lvi, a language of Laos · Brao-Kravet 4 · Brao brb, a language of Laos · Kavet krv, a language of Cambodia · Krung krr, a language of Cambodia · Sou sqq, a language of Laos · Laven 1 · Laven lbo, a language of Laos ·","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
3,"Stieng, Bulo language. Evangelism tools, church planting resources, Christian songs and audio bible study materials. Download free MP3s.",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/sti,"Short audio Bible stories and evangelistic messages that explain salvation and give basic Christian teaching. Each program is a customised and culturally relevant selection of scripts, and may include songs and music.","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
4,"Category:Bulo Stieng language - Wiktionary, the free dictionary",https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Bulo_Stieng_language,This is the main category of the Bulo Stieng language.,"Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
5,"Category:Austroasiatic languages - Wiktionary, the free dictionary",https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Austroasiatic_languages,│ │ ├──── Budeh Stieng (stt) │ │ ├──── Bulo Stieng (sti) │ │ ├──── Central Mnong (cmo) │ │ ├──── Chrau (crw) │ │ ├──── Cua (cua) │ │ ├──── Eastern Mnong (mng) │ │ ├──── Halang Doan (hld) │ │ ├──── Jeh (jeh) │ │ ├──── Jeng (jeg) │ │ ├──── Katua (kta) │ │ ├──── Koho (kpm) │ │ ├──── Kraol (rka) │ │ ├──── Kru'ng (krr) │ │ ├──── Lave (brb) │ │ ├──── Laven (lbo) │ │ ├──── Lawi (lvi) │ │ ├──── Mel-Khaonh (hkn) │ │ ├──── Monom (moo) │ │ ├──── Mạ (cma) │ │ ├───┬ North Bahnaric (mkh-nbn) F ·,"Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
6,"Stieng, Bulo in Cambodia people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15088/CB,"The Stieng people live on the Vietnamese border between Memut in Kompong Cham province, Snoul in Kratie province and Kao Sema in the Mondolkiri province. There are approximately 6,000 Stieng in Cambodia, and nearly 50,000 in Vietnam. They speak two distinct dialects: Budip and Bulo.","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
7,"Stieng, Bulo in Vietnam people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15088/VM,"The Stieng people live on the Vietnamese border between Memut in Kompong Cham province, Snoul in Kratie province and Kao Sema in the Mondolkiri province. There are approximately 6,000 Stieng in Cambodia, and nearly 50,000 in Vietnam. They speak two distinct dialects: Budip and Bulo.","Stieng, Bulo",Austro-Asiatic
